# apps/web/.env.local — the Next app's environment. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
#
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. With none of them set the site builds, renders
# and deploys exactly as it does today: `ConvexClientProvider` renders its
# children and mounts no provider, and `src/proxy.ts` passes every request
# straight through. That is deliberate — the public site must not depend on
# Clerk or Convex being reachable (ADR 006).
#
# The Convex *backend* is configured separately and NOT from this file. Anything
# a Convex function reads at runtime — CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN, GITHUB_TOKEN, … —
# lives in the Convex dashboard, because functions never see this repo's env
# files at all. See packages/convex/README.md for the full one-time setup order,
# and packages/convex/.env.example for the CLI's own local config.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables are inlined into the browser bundle at build time. Two
# consequences: they are public by definition (never put a secret behind that
# prefix), and changing one requires a rebuild, not a restart.


# ─── Site identity and index control ──────────────────────────────────────────

# The production origin. Everything absolute the site emits is built from this:
# `metadataBase` in the root layout (so every canonical link, Open Graph image
# and card URL resolves against it), every entry in /sitemap.xml, the `Sitemap:`
# and `Host:` lines in /robots.txt, and the `@id`s in the JSON-LD graph.
#
# OPTIONAL. Unset it defaults to https://coreybaines.com — ADR 017 settled the
# primary domain, so the default is the real answer rather than a placeholder,
# and a fresh checkout emits correct URLs with no environment at all.
#
# Set it deliberately to the *production* host even on a preview deployment.
# That is the point: a preview whose canonicals point at itself competes with
# the site it is previewing for the same search results. No trailing slash is
# needed (one is stripped if present).
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://coreybaines.com

# The index gate (ADR 018). Ships OFF, and every other value than the exact
# string `true` reads as off — a gate whose failure mode is "indexed the
# unfinished site under Corey's name mid-job-hunt" only gets to fail closed.
#
# While it is off:
#   • /robots.txt is `User-Agent: * / Disallow: /` and names no sitemap
#   • every page carries <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
#
# Set it EXACTLY ONCE, at cutover, on the PRODUCTION deployment — never on a
# preview, and never in a local .env.local. This is the switch that ends ADR
# 018's "build behind a preview URL while spiritdevs.com stays live" window, so
# flipping it is the launch, not a step towards it.
#
# It is inlined at build time (NEXT_PUBLIC_), so it takes effect on the next
# build rather than the next cold start. That is deliberate: a runtime read
# could flip between two ISR revalidations and leave half the prerendered HTML
# on the CDN saying noindex.
#
# `/admin`, `/api`, `/v/*` and `/variants` are excluded from indexing
# unconditionally and are unaffected by this variable in either position.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_INDEXABLE=true


# ─── Convex ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The deployment the browser client talks to, printed by `bunx convex dev` on
# first run and visible in the Convex dashboard.
#   dev:  https://<adjective-animal-000>.convex.cloud
#   prod: https://<adjective-animal-000>.convex.cloud (a different deployment)
#
# Required for any Convex read or write from the browser. Paired with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY below: ConvexClientProvider treats one
# without the other as unconfigured rather than half-configured.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=


# ─── Clerk ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Clerk's browser SDK key, from Clerk dashboard → API keys.
#   dev:  pk_test_…
#   prod: pk_live_…
#
# Read in two places: ConvexClientProvider (to decide whether to mount at all,
# and passed explicitly to ClerkProvider) and src/proxy.ts (half of its
# "is Clerk configured" check).
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Clerk's server key, from the same page. Server-side only — it must never gain
# a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, and nothing in src/components may import it.
#   dev:  sk_test_…
#   prod: sk_live_…
#
# Unlike the publishable key this is read from the process at cold start rather
# than inlined at build, so `src/proxy.ts` is only "configured" when the
# publishable key was present at build *and* this is present at runtime.
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=

# Where Clerk sends an unauthenticated visitor, and where it returns them to.
#
# Both are OPTIONAL and both are only read by Clerk's own machinery — nothing in
# this repo reads them directly. `src/app/admin/(shell)/layout.tsx` redirects to
# a literal `/admin/sign-in` precisely so the gate works whether or not these
# are set.
#
# Set NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL when you want `auth.protect()` in
# src/proxy.ts to send people to this app's sign-in page instead of Clerk's
# hosted one. Note the trap it creates and that src/proxy.ts already handles:
# the proxy must NOT protect the sign-in path, or protecting it redirects to
# itself forever. See UNPROTECTED_PATHS there.
#
# There is deliberately no NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL. ADR 006 — single-user
# admin, any authenticated identity is the admin — so no sign-up route exists,
# and sign-ups should also be turned off in the Clerk dashboard.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=/admin/sign-in
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_FALLBACK_REDIRECT_URL=/admin


# ─── UploadThing (ADR 010) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The single credential UploadThing v7 needs, from the UploadThing dashboard →
# API keys → "V7". It is a base64 blob carrying the app id, region and API key
# together, which is why there is nothing else to set.
#
# SECRET. It authorises writes to the CDN, so it must never gain a NEXT_PUBLIC_
# prefix and must never be imported by anything under src/components.
#
# Read in one place: src/app/api/uploadthing/route.ts, at cold start. Unset, that
# route answers 503 with `{ error: "uploads-not-configured" }` and the admin's
# ImageUpload renders a disabled dropzone that says so. Everything else keeps
# working — media already in a document stays editable, including images the iOS
# app uploaded.
#
# The browser is told *whether* this is set, never its value: the admin layout
# reads it server-side and passes a boolean through AdminConfig. That is why
# there is no public mirror variable to keep in sync.
#
# One consequence of `export const dynamic = "force-dynamic"` in the admin
# layout: this is a runtime read, so setting it takes effect on the next cold
# start rather than requiring a rebuild — unlike every NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable
# above.
UPLOADTHING_TOKEN=


# ─── Not set here, but part of the same wiring ─────────────────────────────────

# CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN
#
#   Deliberately absent from this file. It is the Clerk Frontend API URL that
#   Convex validates admin and iOS JWTs against, and it is read by
#   packages/convex/convex/auth.config.ts — which is evaluated on the Convex
#   side, not here. Set it per Convex deployment:
#
#     cd packages/convex
#     bunx convex env set CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN https://<slug>.clerk.accounts.dev
#     bunx convex env set CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN https://clerk.coreybaines.com --prod
#
#   Setting it in apps/web/.env.local has no effect whatsoever. The Clerk JWT
#   template it comes from must also be named exactly `convex`, or every
#   authenticated request silently reads as signed out.
#
#   Full instructions, in the order they must be done: packages/convex/README.md
